  - [0m[1mWhat happened:[0m The first version wrote the board twice as often and only skipped herdr's[0m[2m[48;2;245;245;245m│[0m[48;2;245;245;245m                                                                          [0m
    pane list on the in-between writes. The performance review showed that each write still [0m[2m[48;2;245;245;245m│[0m[48;2;245;245;245m                                                                          [0m
    did all the costly work again: matching panes to mice and reading every mouse's         [0m[2m[48;2;245;245;245m│[0m[48;2;245;245;245m                                                                          [0m
    transcript. The fix in [0m[38;2;87;105;247mlib/whiska/owl/house.ex[0m builds the full board every two seconds. [0m[2m[48;2;245;245;245m│[0m[48;2;245;245;245m                                                                          [0m
    The writes in between call [0m[38;2;87;105;247mWatch.retime/2[0m, which redoes only the elapsed time and the   [0m[2m[48;2;245;245;245m│[0m[48;2;245;245;245m                                                                          [0m
    "picked up … ago" age, from timestamps saved on each row.                               [0m[2m[48;2;245;245;245m│[0m[48;2;245;245;245m                                                                          [0m
  - [0m[1mThe principle:[0m When only one value has to update faster, update just that value. Running[0m[2m[48;2;245;245;245m│[0m[48;2;245;245;245m                                                                          [0m
    the whole pipeline more often is the costly way to get it.                              [0m[2m[48;2;245;245;245m│[0m[48;2;245;245;245m                                                                          [0m
  - [0m[1mWhy it matters:[0m The owl's extra cost went from "everything, twice as often" to one      [0m[2m[48;2;245;245;245m│[0m[48;2;245;245;245m                                                                          [0m
    render and one file write per second. The format is still spelled in one place,         [0m[2m[48;2;245;245;245m│[0m[48;2;245;245;245m                                                                          [0m
    [0m[38;2;87;105;247mformat_uptime[0m, so the board and [0m[38;2;87;105;247mwhiska mice[0m can't disagree.                             [0m[2m[48;2;245;245;245m│[0m[48;2;245;245;245m                                                                          [0m
